    background: `Sedona Red Rock Sanctuary is an upscale 110-casita desert resort situated on 25 secluded acres of red sandstone canyons in Arizona. Designed with adobe architecture, meditation courtyards, and an award-winning 15,000-square-foot spa, the sanctuary currently operates as a traditional luxury leisure hotel with an ADR of $520 and 70% occupancy. While guests appreciate the scenic vistas, average length of stay has remained stagnant at 2.1 nights, and secondary spend on wellness services averages only $95 per guest day despite world-class spa facilities.

Recent consumer research published by the Global Wellness Institute reveals that wellness tourism is expanding at more than 12% annually, with travelers seeking structured, transformational retreats rather than passive weekend getaways. Wealthy professionals, tech executives, and high-stress creatives are actively paying premium rates for four-to-six-day curated immersions that promise stress reduction, circadian restoration, mental clarity, and gut-health optimization.

Recognizing this market shift, property ownership has decided to launch a dedicated, all-inclusive four-day, three-night retreat brand: "The Sedona Mind & Horizon Immersive." Rather than offering piecemeal a la carte spa treatments, this program will bundle private casita lodging, personalized Ayurvedic or plant-forward chef-curated nutrition, daily guided canyon sunrise meditation, private breathwork sessions, sound baths, and bespoke restorative body therapies.

However, pivoting a commercial leisure resort into an authentic wellness sanctuary creates significant marketing challenges. The marketing team must communicate the clinical and restorative credibility of the facilitators without sounding clinical or intimidating. Furthermore, the pricing structure must reflect high luxury exclusivity—targeted at $3,800 to $4,500 per single attendee—while guaranteeing that guests who purchase the retreat experience a seamless, tranquil journey untouched by standard leisure or wedding guests who may be staying on property.

You and your partner (serving as the Wellness Product Marketing Director and Resort Experience Coordinator) are meeting with the Vice President of Resort Operations and Commercial Programming (played by the judge). You must present a comprehensive market launch strategy for "The Sedona Mind & Horizon Immersive." Your proposal must detail target guest personas, structured daily itineraries, all-inclusive pricing architecture, promotional partnerships with respected wellness practitioners, and digital storytelling campaigns that drive high-ticket retreat registrations.`,
    challenge: 'Develop a luxury market launch plan for an all-inclusive 4-day Mindful Wellness Retreat program. Present guest psychographic profiling, all-inclusive pricing tiers, operational guest segmentation, and high-converting wellness marketing funnels.',
