    background: `Aura Hospitality Group is a fast-growing regional hotel collection operating 18 upscale lifestyle properties across six states in the American Sunbelt, comprising 3,200 total guest rooms and $160 million in annual room revenues. Two years ago, Aura launched its proprietary mobile app, "Aura Key," featuring mobile check-in, digital Bluetooth room keys, concierge messaging, and a basic points-based loyalty program: "Aura Rewards."

Despite investing over $800,000 in mobile app development, adoption metrics remain stubbornly low. Currently, fewer than 14% of eligible hotel guests download the app before arrival, and only 22% of active loyalty members open the app after checking out. Most guests view Aura Rewards as just another generic, forgettable points program where it takes ten expensive hotel nights simply to earn a single free breakfast voucher. Consequently, member churn is high, and 58% of past guests continue booking subsequent stays through third-party OTAs rather than through the mobile app.

Recent behavioral economics data suggests that younger business and leisure travelers (aged 24-45) engage far more deeply with gamified reward systems that incorporate progress bars, surprise-and-delight rewards, badge accomplishments, and experiential challenges, rather than slow, transactional point accumulation. Rival international chains are already rolling out digital badges for visiting multiple brand flags or completing fitness milestones on property.

The Executive Committee has approved a $150,000 commercial growth initiative to revamp Aura Rewards through dynamic mobile gamification. The corporate goal is to increase mobile app adoption from 14% to 45% of total guests, raise direct mobile rebooking rates by 30%, and boost Customer Lifetime Value (CLV) by $420 per active loyalty member over the next 18 months.

You and your partner (serving as the Chief Customer Officer and Digital Loyalty Product Manager) are meeting with the Executive Vice President of Commercial Strategy and Brand Operations (played by the judge). You must present an innovative gamification and mobile app adoption blueprint titled "Aura Explorer: The Gamified Stay." Your presentation must detail gamified achievement mechanics, front desk associate download incentive programs, push-notification in-stay engagement, data security safeguards, and financial modeling demonstrating ROI from reduced OTA commission leakage.`,
